      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant 496800 Full-Time Office of VP Student Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Department : Dean of Students Salary : Commensurate with Experience and Education Description : The Administrative Assistant provides administrative and operational support to a department, division, or academic unit within the University. This position serves as a key point of contact for faculty, staff, students, and visitors while ensuring efficient office operations and excellent customer service. The Administrative Assistant performs a variety of clerical, organizational, and administrative tasks to support the department’s goals and the University's mission. Duties: Administrative Support: Provide administrative support to department leadership, faculty, and staff. Manage calendars, schedule meetings, and coordinate appointments. Prepare, edit, and distribute correspondence, reports, presentations, and other documents. Answer phones, respond to emails, and direct inquiries to appropriate personnel. Maintain office supplies and coordinate equipment maintenance as needed. Customer Service and Communication: Serve as the first point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Provide accurate information regarding departmental services and procedures. Assist with resolving routine questions and concerns professionally and courteously. Support communication efforts through email, newsletters, or departmental announcements as needed. Records Management: Maintain departmental files, records, and databases. Ensure accuracy and confidentiality of student, employee, and departmental information. Assist with data entry, record retention, and document management activities. Generate routine reports and retrieve information as requested. Meeting and Event Coordination: Schedule and coordinate meetings, workshops, and special events. Assist with tracking expenses and monitoring office resources. Support procurement and vendor communication activities. May assist with departmental projects and initiatives and perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. Minimum of one year of administrative, clerical, or office support experience. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and standard office software. Preferred Qualifications: Associate's degree. Experience working in a college, university, or educational environment. Experience coordinating events, meetings, or office operations. Familiarity with student information systems or higher education administrative processes. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong customer service and interpersonal skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Attention to detail and accuracy in administrative work. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong problem-solving and organizational skills. All positions at the University of Houston System are security-sensitive and require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cya