      "title": "Department Business Administrator",
      "description": "Department Business Administrator  - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Department Business Administrator 496805 Full-Time Business Operations Add to favorites View favorites Department : Business Operations Salary : Commensurate with education and experience. Description : The Department Business Administrator (DBA) manages and administers business, financial and non-academic operations of a moderately complex department or for multiple departments including budget planning, financial oversight and monitoring; human resources business processes, staff, and faculty affairs. The DBA provides functional supervision of coordinators and serves as the liaison for Senior Leadership, directors, faculty and staff with other university departments and offices. Duties: Manages budgets, including managing and supporting annual budget preparations; monitoring and advising department budgets and accounts; preparing budgetary and personnel reports, analyses and projections. Monitors all budgets in the department(s) including fee revenue, income operations and external programs. Oversees and approves all HR business processes for the department(s) which includes but is not limited to human resources and payroll, and position budget management. Reviews and approves the reconciliation of accounting records with university reports/financial statements and prepares recurring financial/budget reports for internal purposes. Provides functional and direct supervision of financial and business operations staff. Manages the procurement operations and contract administration for the department(s). Monitors all budgets in the college including fee revenue, income operations and external programs. Serves as a resource to the Associate/Assistant VPs, department heads, etc. and provides liaison to university as well as to external units and performs related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related field. Minimum five years of directly related job experience. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related field. Previous work-related experience in a higher education institution. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to handle multiple projects and tasks concurrently. Strong proficiency in financial software, spreadsheets, communication, problem-solving, and attention to detail. Knowledge of budgeting principles, accounting procedures, and financial reporting. Ability to work within a team-oriented environment and adapt to changing institutional priorities. Strong verbal and written communication for interdepartmental coordination. Ability to identify issues and implement solutions regarding operational inefficiencies or student/staff needs. Expertise in Microsoft Office Suite (especially Excel), project management tools, and database management. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees and leaders at all levels throughout the University. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Op