      "title": "Patient Services Specialist",
      "description": "Patient Services Specialist - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Patient Services Specialist 496698 Full-Time Health Services Add to favorites View favorites Department : Health Services Salary : Commensurate with education and experience. Description : The Patient Services Specialist is responsible for supporting Health Services professional staff in the daily operations. Serves as the initial contact for students, faculty, staff and visitors seeking services or information from Health Services. This position provides excellent customer/patient services support including managing the patient management information system, telephone coverage, appointment schedules, and assists with the Student Health Insurance Plan program. Duties: Primary responsibilities include patient check-in; verifying demographics; collecting copay's/self-pay balances; confirmation appointment calls and answering multi-phone lines. Acts as the liaison between the student and the student health insurance provider including telephone interactions, resolves International Student Health Insurance Plan waiver claims, orientation presentations with educational resources. Provides clinical assistance with recording vital signs to input in EMR system. Receives and confirms inventory and purchases of pharmaceutical and over-the-counter medications, and laboratory and office supplies. Creates and maintains office policies and procedures, as well as evaluates facility needs, with the collaboration of the Health Services Director. Assists with off-campus/distance education sites (i.e. Pearland campus) for mobile flu-shot clinic, blood pressure screenings, and other educational programs. Participates in orientation and new student programs. Manages cash handling and processes daily cash deposits and performs related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: High School diploma Minimum of two years of experience in medical reception or other related office experience. Preferred Qualifications: Associate's degree from an accredited program. Three years of experience with electronic health/medical record management. Experience with supporting patients, students, staff and/or faculty. Electric Medical Record system and CPL laboratory portal experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of Medical and ICD-10 health insurance billing practices and procedures. Knowledge of budget management. Ability to effectively use Microsoft Office suite of products, PeopleSoft, and Electronic Medical Record system. Knowledge of health and medical regulations and practices (HIPAA). Ability to pay close attention to detail while maintaining high level of confidentiality. Strong office organizational, planning and management skills. Ability to work an electric BP Monitor and a battery operated Temperature Probe (report findings). Must have clear, precise, and effective oral/written communication skills. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transp