      "title": "Executive Director, Business Operations",
      "description": "Executive Director, Business Operations - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Executive Director, Business Operations 496685 Full-Time Business Operations Add to favorites View favorites Department : Business Operations Salary : Commensurate with Experience and Education Description: The Executive Director, Business Operations reports to the Associate Vice President of Business Operations. The Executive Director aids in the oversight of university-wide financial planning, budgeting, business operations, compliance, and human resources management. The Executive Director serves as a resource to Director, Business Operations for all divisions within the University. Duties: Assists in the oversight of financial and budget operations, ensuring financial accountability and compliance with state, university, and external funding agency guidelines, and assisting in the development and implementation of university-wide business processes and best practices. Directly oversees the Director(s) of Division Business Operations. Participates in onboarding/training for new business officers. Develops comprehensive goals, objectives, and plans guiding the operations of each functional unit, ensuring that established goals and objectives are communicated and obtained. Provides assistance to the Administration and Finance Leadership in the implementation of organizational decisions. This includes working on special projects, developing training workshops, and generating custom reports. Serves as a resource to the Director(s) of Division Business Operations in each division for all administration, budget, finance, and human resources-related inquiries. Assists the Executive Director of Planning and Budget with the annual budgeting process. Monitors budget and equity balances for the various divisions. Serves as primary reviewer to conduct compliance audits for procurement and contractual documents, including contracts, amendments, MOUs, affiliation agreements, extension agreements, and revenue agreements within all Divisions. Manages databases in Finance & Administration, including the division control totals for all divisions. Analyzes financial data using Data Warehouse, PeopleSoft queries, and the Student Dashboard and produces customized reports on Division/College financials for use by executive leadership. Serves as liaison with executives and administrative offices regarding fiscal and operational issues. Interacts with UH System, other UHS components, UHCL, Coordinating Board, and various State universities on fiscal and policy matters. Serves as main contact for auditors during audits of business operations. Conducts division-wide mock audits to ensure compliance with state and university policies and procedures. Assists the Associate Vice President in Business Operations with departments of general accounting, student business services, auxiliary enterprises, procurement, accounts payable, and travel operations. Performs related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Master's degree Minimum ten years of directly related job experience. Experience supervising professional staff. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to think strategically while executing operationally in a complex and centralized environment. Excellent communication skills with the ability to present financial information to non-financial audiences and executive leadership. Strong leadership, collaboration, and relationship-building skills across University-wide stakeholders. High level of attention to detail, organization, and ability to manage multiple priorities. Exercise critical thinking and sound decision-making through observing, analyzing, inferring, communicating, and problem-solving in challenging situations with ethics, tact, confidence, and diplomacy. Organize and prioritize a variety of projects and multiple tasks in an effective and timely manner; organize own work, set priorities, and meet critical time deadlines. Review situations accurately and determine appropriate course of action using judgment according to established policies and procedures; understand scope of authority in making independent decisions. Establish, maintain, and foster positive and effective working relationships with those contacted in the course of work. All positions at the University of Houston System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Apply now First Name (required) 2c46b3b8 Last Name (required) 71314ecc Email (required) d814e43e Cell number 0e256780 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) A