      "title": "Financial Coordinator",
      "description": "Financial Coordinator - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Financial Coordinator 496520 Full-Time Business Operations Add to favorites View favorites Department :  Business Operations Salary : Commensurate with experience and education Description: The Financial Coordinator provides professional-level fiscal, analytical, and support for assigned areas by overseeing business operations, including submitting transactional and budgetary data, and advising stakeholders on fiscal decisions. The role ensures compliance, financial stewardship, and continuous improvement of business processes in support of assigned areas. Duties: Maintains and reconciles financial accounts, monitors revenue and expenditures for assigned areas. Processes financial and payroll transactions and personnel expenditures on departmental operating accounts. Prepares journal vouchers needed to effect changes in accounts. May prepare billing, financial reports, and/or invoices for various foundations and institutions. Reconciles financial accounts for a department or office to the monthly statements provided by the University. Prepares monthly and quarterly financial reports for department management. May train others regarding preparation of financial documents. Researches and corrects reconciliation discrepancies with reallocations and journal vouchers and performs related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Associate's degree Minimum three years of job-related experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field Previous work-related experience in a higher education institution. Experience with auditing or financial analysis. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated attention to detail and ability to manage multiple requests in a structured environment. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Strong skills concerning attention to detail and accuracy in reviewing and processing documentation. Ability to organize, prioritize, and track multiple requests in a structured, deadline-driven environment. Demonstrated follow-through and accountability in monitoring transactions and ensuring completion of assigned tasks. Ability to maintain professionalism and composure while serving as a first point of contact for internal and external stakeholders. Ability to maintain organized electronic and shared records to support compliance and operational transparency. All positions at the University of Houston System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. App