    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/manager-health-services-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Manager, Health Services",
      "description": "Manager, Health Services - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Manager, Health Services 496581 Full-Time Health Services Add to favorites View favorites Department : Health Services Salary : Commensurate with experience and education Description : The Manager, Health Services oversees the daily operations of the campus health services clinic and provides supervision and support to departmental staff. Ensures efficient administrative processes, including scheduling, front-office coordination, workflow management, and compliance with campus policies. Serves as the primary point of contact for departmental inquiries and operational needs, allowing medical staff to focus on delivering high-quality patient care. This role plays a key part in creating a well-organized, student-centered, and responsive clinic environment. Duties: Provides administrative leadership for unit strategic planning, budget management, and coordination of agreements with external vendors or service providers. Conducts assessments to ensure clinic operations align with divisional and institutional goals and objectives. Promotes and integrate student health and wellness initiatives across campus, supporting university recruitment, retention, and overall wellbeing efforts. Oversees clinic operations to ensure efficiency, compliance with federal and state regulations, and alignment with institutional policies. Oversees the management, facility and equipment maintenance, operation, and staffing schedules of the clinic. Stays informed about and ensure compliance with UHCL policies, regulations, and best practices in college health and student affairs. Ensures adherence to local health regulations, including the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) and the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA). Reviews and audits records of clinic operations and medical providers for quality assurance. Manages the creation and updates of all policies, procedures, medical protocols, and forms. Provides direction in the hiring, training, development, supervision, and evaluation of professional and support staff for the department. Manages and oversees the development and execution of the department's graphics, promotional materials, and outreach initiatives. This includes print and digital media, website content, online resources, and other marketing efforts to effectively communicate the department's services and offerings. Collaborates with other campus offices to support and coordinate institutional initiatives. Remains current with trends and innovations in college health and clinic operations. Plans for potential crises and ensures business continuity in the event of building or system disruptions. Serves on university, divisional, and system-level committees that support the efforts of health services for UHCL students and performs related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, healthcare, or a related field Minimum three years of experience supervising full-time employees. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in business, healthcare, or a related field. Five years of experience working in a health-related environment such as a clinic or hospital. Knowledge, Skills and abilities: Knowledge of administrative and operational management principles, including workflow coordination, staffing practices, and process optimization to ensure efficient clinic functioning. Knowledge of customer service concepts, privacy standards, and front-office procedures necessary to support a student-centered health services environment and maintain compliance with institutional policies. Ability to direct collection, analysis, and interpretation of statistics relevant to program planning. Proficiency in using electronic health record (EHR) systems and medical documentation platforms to support accurate recordkeeping, appointment management, and clinic operations. Strong ability to utilize administrative software and data management tools, including scheduling systems, reporting platforms, and workflow applications, to ensure clinic processes and staff coordination are efficient. Ability to communicate clearly and professionally, both orally and in writing, to effectively support staff, students, and campus partners. Ability to assess situations, identify solutions, and make sound decisions in a fast-paced clinic environment, demonstrating strong problem-solving and interpersonal skills. All positions at the University of Houston System are security-sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Apply now First Name (required) 1df586cb Last Name (required) f77287c8 Email (required) 5f831e86 Cell number 4e4d9a5b